IMPORT prelude

-- Internationally Protected Persons Act 2008 (Singapore) -- who is an internationally protected person (s 3(1)), relevant
-- premises (s 2), offences committed outside Singapore against such persons, their premises and vehicles (ss 4, 5, 7, First and
-- Second Schedules), threats made in or outside Singapore (s 6), the presumption of knowledge (s 8), the duty of everyone in
-- Singapore to disclose information to the police and the shield for good-faith disclosure (s 9), and the Public Prosecutor's
-- consent (s 12).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/7/2025", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IPPA2008.txt. The latest
-- amendments annotated are Act 3 of 2021 wef 01/07/2025 (First Schedule items 2 and 3 deleted, item 32 annotated) and Act 17 of
-- 2022 wef 01/07/2022 (s 11, extradition). Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit: the arrangement of sections at the top
-- is one out of step (it lists a blank "1." and puts "Short title" at 2).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0125 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has yet asked a sharper question. For
-- an ordinary person in Singapore the answer is mainly s 9 (a duty to tell the police, punishable by $50,000 or 5 years) and s 6
-- (threats made in Singapore); the rest reaches acts done abroad.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Minister's certificate (s 3(2)) beyond a comment; mutual legal assistance (s 10) and extradition (s 11), save
-- that both deem the offences not to be of a political character; amendment of the Schedules (s 13); the punishments for the
-- scheduled offences themselves, which live in the Penal Code and the other Acts named and were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Internationally Protected Persons Act 2008 -- offences`

§§ `3(1) -- internationally protected person`

-- s 3(1): "(a) a Head of State, including any member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a Head of State ..., a head
-- of a government or a minister responsible for foreign affairs, whenever he or she is outside the State in which he or she holds that
-- position or office; (b) a member of the family of a person referred to in paragraph (a) who is accompanying the person; (c) a
-- representative or official of a State or an official or agent of an international organisation of an intergovernmental character
-- who, at the time and place of the alleged offence, is entitled under international law to special protection from any attack on his
-- or her person, freedom or dignity; or (d) a member of the family of a person referred to in paragraph (c) who forms part of the
-- person's household."
-- s 3(2): the Minister's written certificate is "prima facie evidence" of the matters stated.
--
-- The family tests differ: under (b) the family member must be ACCOMPANYING; under (d) must be part of the HOUSEHOLD. INFERENCE: an
-- office-holder in paragraph (a) is also "a representative or official of a State", so may qualify under (c) where entitled to
-- special protection; and a paragraph (b) family member qualifies only while the paragraph (a) person is outside his or her State.
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `a Head of State`
    `a member of a collegial Head of State`
    `a head of government`
    `a minister for foreign affairs`
    `another minister`
    `a diplomatic agent`
    `an official of an intergovernmental organisation`
    `a private individual`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a paragraph (a) office` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `a Head of State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of a collegial Head of State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a head of government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a minister for foreign affairs` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office,
      `is outside the State of office` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is entitled to special protection under international law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a family member rather than the office-holder` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `accompanies the office-holder` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `forms part of the office-holder's household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an internationally protected person` IF
        (    `is a paragraph (a) office` `the office`
         AND `is outside the State of office`
         AND ((NOT `is a family member rather than the office-holder`) OR `accompanies the office-holder`))
    OR  (    (NOT (`the office` EQUALS `a private individual`))
         AND `is entitled to special protection under international law`
         AND ((NOT `is a family member rather than the office-holder`) OR `forms part of the office-holder's household`))

§§ `2 -- relevant premises`

-- s 2: "'relevant premises' means premises at which an internationally protected person resides or is staying or which he or she uses
-- for the purpose of carrying out his or her functions as such person"; "'vehicle' includes any means of conveyance."
DECLARE PremisesUse IS ONE OF
    `where the protected person resides`
    `where the protected person is staying`
    `used for the protected person's functions`
    `a restaurant the protected person once dined at`

GIVEN `the use` IS A PremisesUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `are relevant premises` IF
    NOT (`the use` EQUALS `a restaurant the protected person once dined at`)

§§ `First and Second Schedules`

-- First Schedule (offences against internationally protected persons) includes: s 4 Corrosive and Explosive Substances and
-- Offensive Weapons Act 1958; s 3 Hostage-Taking Act 2010; s 3 Kidnapping Act 1961; Penal Code ss 302 (murder), 304, 325 (voluntarily
-- causing grievous hurt), 326 to 331, 342 (wrongful confinement), 343, 344 (as in force before 1 January 2020), 346 to 348, 354A
-- ("Outraging modesty in certain circumstances"), 356, 357, 363 (kidnapping), 363A, 364, 364A (as in force before 21 November 2010),
-- 365 to 368, 375 (rape), 376, 376A. Items 2 and 3 "[Deleted by Act 3 of 2021 wef 01/07/2025]".
-- NOT listed: Penal Code s 323 (simple hurt), s 352 (simple assault), s 354 (outrage of modesty without the s 354A circumstances),
-- s 506 (criminal intimidation). The listing is read from the deposit; the descriptions of the unlisted sections are from general
-- knowledge of the Penal Code, which was not retrieved.
DECLARE PersonOffence IS ONE OF
    `murder (Penal Code s 302)`
    `voluntarily causing grievous hurt (Penal Code s 325)`
    `rape (Penal Code s 375)`
    `kidnapping (Penal Code s 363)`
    `hostage-taking (Hostage-Taking Act s 3)`
    `wrongful confinement (Penal Code s 342)`
    `outraging modesty in certain circumstances (Penal Code s 354A)`
    `voluntarily causing hurt (Penal Code s 323)`
    `outraging modesty (Penal Code s 354)`
    `criminal intimidation (Penal Code s 506)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A PersonOffence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a First Schedule offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `voluntarily causing hurt (Penal Code s 323)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `outraging modesty (Penal Code s 354)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `criminal intimidation (Penal Code s 506)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Second Schedule (offences against premises or vehicles): Explosive Substances Act 1924 ss 3 ("Causing explosion likely to endanger
-- property"), 4; Penal Code ss 426 (mischief), 427, 430A (as in force before 1 January 2020), 435 ("Mischief by fire or explosive
-- substance with intent to cause damage"), 436 to 440. NOT listed: criminal trespass, house-breaking, theft.
DECLARE PropertyOffence IS ONE OF
    `mischief (Penal Code s 426)`
    `mischief by fire or explosive substance (Penal Code s 435)`
    `causing an explosion likely to endanger property (Explosive Substances Act s 3)`
    `criminal trespass (Penal Code s 447)`
    `theft (Penal Code s 379)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A PropertyOffence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Second Schedule offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `criminal trespass (Penal Code s 447)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `theft (Penal Code s 379)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4, 8(1) -- offences against persons outside Singapore`

-- s 4(1): "Any person who commits outside Singapore any act -- (a) to or in relation to a person whom the firstmentioned person knows
-- to be an internationally protected person; and (b) which, if committed in Singapore, would have constituted an offence specified in
-- the First Schedule, shall be guilty of that offence" with the same punishment; (2) "may be dealt with as if the offence had been
-- committed in Singapore".
-- s 8(1): once the act against an internationally protected person is proved, "it is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that the
-- accused knew". So knowledge is not a fact the prosecution proves; LACK of knowledge is the accused's to prove.
-- Nothing in s 4 requires the offender or the victim to be Singaporean. An act IN Singapore is not caught by s 4 at all: it is the
-- scheduled offence itself under the Penal Code or other Act.
GIVEN `the act was done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim is an internationally protected person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence` IS A PersonOffence,
      `the accused proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence under section 4` IF
        `the act was done outside Singapore`
    AND `the victim is an internationally protected person`
    AND `is a First Schedule offence` `the offence`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved lack of knowledge`)

§§ `5, 8(2) -- offences against premises or vehicles outside Singapore`

-- s 5(1): an act outside Singapore "(a) to or in relation to -- (i) premises which he or she knows to be relevant premises; or (ii) a
-- vehicle which he or she knows is used by an internationally protected person; (b) which is likely to endanger the person or liberty
-- of the internationally protected person; and (c) which, if committed in Singapore, would have constituted an offence specified in the
-- Second Schedule". s 8(2): knowledge presumed unless the contrary is proved.
DECLARE Target IS ONE OF
    `relevant premises`
    `a vehicle used by an internationally protected person`
    `other property`

GIVEN `the act was done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the target` IS A Target,
      `the act is likely to endanger the protected person's person or liberty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence` IS A PropertyOffence,
      `the accused proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence under section 5` IF
        `the act was done outside Singapore`
    AND (NOT (`the target` EQUALS `other property`))
    AND `the act is likely to endanger the protected person's person or liberty`
    AND `is a Second Schedule offence` `the offence`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved lack of knowledge`)

§§ `6, 8(3) -- threats, in or outside Singapore`

-- s 6(1): "Any person who, in or outside Singapore, threatens to commit an act which is -- (a) an offence specified in the First
-- Schedule or under section 4 to or in relation to a person whom the firstmentioned person knows to be an internationally protected
-- person; or (b) an offence specified in the Second Schedule or under section 5 to or in relation to -- (i) premises which he or she
-- knows to be relevant premises; or (ii) a vehicle which he or she knows is used by an internationally protected person, and which, if
-- committed, is likely to endanger the person or liberty of the internationally protected person". s 8(3): knowledge presumed.
--
-- READING TAKEN: the closing words "and which, if committed, is likely to endanger ..." (printed in the deposit with a stray "(b)"
-- label) are read as qualifying limb (b) only, as the same words qualify only premises and vehicles in s 5. The other reading,
-- applying them to threats against a person too, is open.
GIVEN `the threatened person is an internationally protected person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the threatened offence` IS A PersonOffence,
      `the accused proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a threat against a person is an offence under section 6` IF
        `the threatened person is an internationally protected person`
    AND `is a First Schedule offence` `the threatened offence`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved lack of knowledge`)

GIVEN `the target` IS A Target,
      `the threatened offence` IS A PropertyOffence,
      `the act if committed is likely to endanger the protected person's person or liberty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accused proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a threat against premises or a vehicle is an offence under section 6` IF
        (NOT (`the target` EQUALS `other property`))
    AND `is a Second Schedule offence` `the threatened offence`
    AND `the act if committed is likely to endanger the protected person's person or liberty`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved lack of knowledge`)

-- s 6(1): "a fine or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding -- (c) 7 years; or (d) the term of imprisonment to which a person would
-- be liable for the offence constituted by committing the act threatened ..., whichever is the lesser, or to both". (2): where no term
-- is prescribed for the threatened offence, "a fine or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years, or ... both".
-- No maximum fine is stated in either subsection.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS
    IF a < b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `the threatened offence carries a term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `its maximum term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for a threat` MEANS
    IF `the threatened offence carries a term of imprisonment`
    THEN `the lesser of` 7 `its maximum term in years`
    ELSE 7

§§ `7, 8(4) -- abetment, conspiracy and attempt outside Singapore`

-- s 7: a person who, outside Singapore, does an act which "if committed in Singapore, would constitute an abetment of or a conspiracy or
-- an attempt to commit -- (a) an offence specified in the First Schedule or under section 4, where the offence is or is to be committed
-- to or in relation to a person whom the firstmentioned person knows to be an internationally protected person; ... is deemed to commit
-- the act in Singapore and may be dealt with accordingly." s 8(4): knowledge presumed. Limb (b), premises and vehicles, is not encoded.
GIVEN `the act was done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act would be an abetment, conspiracy or attempt in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the intended victim is an internationally protected person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the intended offence` IS A PersonOffence,
      `the accused proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 7` IF
        `the act was done outside Singapore`
    AND `the act would be an abetment, conspiracy or attempt in Singapore`
    AND `the intended victim is an internationally protected person`
    AND `is a First Schedule offence` `the intended offence`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved lack of knowledge`)

§§ `9 -- the duty to tell the police`

-- s 9(4): "'relevant offence' means -- (a) an offence specified in the First Schedule committed to or in relation to an internationally
-- protected person; (b) an offence specified in the Second Schedule committed to or in relation to relevant premises or a vehicle used
-- by an internationally protected person; (c) an offence under section 4 or 5; or (d) an abetment of or a conspiracy or an attempt".
-- Limb (a) has no place requirement and no knowledge requirement: an ordinary First Schedule offence in Singapore against a visiting
-- foreign minister is a relevant offence. Only limb (a) is encoded here.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A PersonOffence,
      `the victim is an internationally protected person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a relevant offence under section 9(4)(a)` IF
    `the victim is an internationally protected person` AND `is a First Schedule offence` `the offence`

-- s 9(1): "Every person in Singapore who has information which the person knows or believes may be of material assistance -- (a) in
-- preventing the commission by another person of a relevant offence; or (b) in securing the apprehension, prosecution or conviction of
-- another person, in Singapore, for an offence involving the commission, preparation or instigation of a relevant offence, and who fails
-- to disclose the information immediately to a police officer shall be guilty of an offence" -- "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or ... both".
-- The text gives NO reasonable-excuse defence. Telling someone other than a police officer, or telling the police later, is not
-- disclosure "immediately to a police officer".
GIVEN `is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information concerns a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows or believes it may materially assist in preventing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows or believes it may materially assist apprehension, prosecution or conviction in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed it immediately to a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to disclose is an offence under section 9` IF
        `is in Singapore`
    AND `the information concerns a relevant offence`
    AND (    `knows or believes it may materially assist in preventing the offence`
         OR  `knows or believes it may materially assist apprehension, prosecution or conviction in Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `disclosed it immediately to a police officer`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for failing to disclose` MEANS 50000

-- s 9(2): "No criminal or civil proceedings shall lie against a person for any disclosure made in good faith under this section."
-- (3): such a person "is not to be treated as being in breach of any restriction upon the disclosure of information imposed by law,
-- contract or rules of professional conduct."
GIVEN `made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is shielded from proceedings and from confidentiality restrictions` IF
    `made in good faith`

§§ `12 -- the Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- s 12: "A prosecution under this Act must not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `an offence under this Act is made out` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Public Prosecutor institutes or consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `an offence under this Act is made out` AND `the Public Prosecutor institutes or consents`
